    "arrows": [],
    "story": [
      "the lines form a grid: the three header words are options (columns: BullMQ (today), Postgres SKIP LOCKED, SQS) and the words down the left are criteria (rows); each short word in a cell is that option's answer for that row, known only from where it sits",
      "for example 'none' is Postgres's ops cost, 'extra Redis' is BullMQ's, '$ + IAM' is SQS's; '15 min max' is SQS's delayed jobs",
      "SQS's delayed-jobs cell was '?' and became '15 min max' when they remembered the delay cap",
      "the '?' cells are what they do not know: delayed jobs on Postgres (they think it needs a run_at column) and how to see stuck jobs on SQS",
      "the 'exactly once' row is struck through with a pen line: dropped as a criterion because none of the options give it and handlers must be idempotent anyway",
      "the circled cell is ops cost × Postgres ('none'): the deciding criterion, said aloud and typed in the note",
      "the underline under the Postgres header means they are leaning towards Postgres, conditional on the delayed-jobs '?'",
      "the BullMQ header is blue because it is today's setup, the baseline (said aloud)"
    ],
    "partner_should_ask_about": [
      "how delayed jobs would work on Postgres (the '?' in that cell)",
      "how stuck jobs would be seen on SQS",
      "whether any job today relies on delays longer than 15 minutes"
    ]
  }
